      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11481659::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11481659::web::013::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed nanobands will be intragranular and alter the dislocation structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11481659::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11481659::web::013::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The annealing treatment refines the intragranular microstructure by precipitating Ti-rich nanobands.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11481659::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11481659::web::013::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti-rich nanobands act as obstacles to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoband formation shifts deformation from screw-dislocation-dominated behavior to edge-dislocation-dominated behavior at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Edge dislocations have a less steep thermal-activation dependence than screw dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A transition to edge-dislocation-dominated deformation will improve high-temperature yield-strength retention.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1273 K, the annealed TiVNbTa alloy will have significantly higher yield strength than the 330 MPa untreated baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11481659::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11481659::web::013::conclusion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The yield-strength increase at 1273 K could range from tens of MPa to approximately 200 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11481659::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
